<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rif War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/1926">1926</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Third Rif War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rif War was fought from 1921 to 1926 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, joined by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1925, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> tribes of the Rif mountains in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-el-krim">Abd el-Krim</a>, who founded the Republic of the Rif. The Spanish disaster at Annual in July 1921 cost thousands of lives and contributed to Primo de Rivera's coup in 1923. A Franco-Spanish landing at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hoceima">Alhucemas</a> in 1925 turned the war, and Abd el-Krim surrendered in May 1926.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rif-war.jpg" alt="Rif War" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 296cherry · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balanced_infobox_collage_for_Rif_War.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
